    "formula": "Thermal resistance network: R_ja = R_jc + R_cb + R_ba; R_jc = 8 K/W (junction to case), R_cb = 5 K/W (case to board), R_ba = 12 K/W (board to ambient); R_ja = 8 + 5 + 12 = 25 K/W; Junction temperature: T_j = T_a + Q × R_ja = 298 + 5 × 25 = 423 K (150°C); Board temperature rise: ΔT_board = Q × R_ba = 5 × 12 = 60 K; Average board temperature: T_board = 298 + 60 = 358 K (85°C); Thermal via array contribution: R_via_array = 1/(n × k_cu × A_via/L_via) = 1/(64 × 385 × π×(0.00015)²/0.0016) = 1/(64 × 385 × 4.42e-8) = 1/(1.09e-3) = 917 K/W per via array; Effective R_ba with vias ≈ 10 K/W (reduced from 12); With vias: T_j = 298 + 5 × (8+5+10) = 298 + 115 = 413 K (140°C); Maximum PCB temperature gradient: ΔT_max ≈ 15 K across board",
